# Local development needs none of these — vite.config.ts proxies /api to
# http://localhost:5080 and the SPA calls /api relative.

# --- Static deployment (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, S3 + CDN) ----------------
# Netlify is a static host: it cannot run the .NET API. Deploy the API
# separately (Azure Container Apps, Render, Fly.io, Railway, a VM) and then
# choose ONE of the two options below.

# Option A — proxy through the static host. Preferred: the browser stays on one
# origin, so there is no CORS to configure. Set this as a build environment
# variable on the host, not in this file.
# API_PROXY_TARGET=https://futuretech-api.example.com

# Option B — call the API directly on its own origin. The API must then list
# this site in Cors:Origins, e.g. Cors__Origins__0=https://your-site.netlify.app
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://futuretech-api.example.com/api

# --- Dev override ----------------------------------------------------------
# Point the dev proxy somewhere other than localhost:5080.
# VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:5080
